man:stylusnexus/agent-plugins:
{
  "name": "stylus-nexus",
  "owner": {
    "name": "Stylus Nexus"
  },
  "description": "Stylus Nexus plugins for Claude Code + Codex.",
  "plugins": [
    {
      "name": "second-opinion",
      "source": "./plugins/second-opinion",
      "description": "Five skills built on one premise: a single model's confident answer is not evidence. llm-council runs a question through five advisors who analyse independently before synthesis; plan-arbiter compares, judges, and merges competing plans rather than picking one on vibes; spec-review checks a spec's claims against the real codebase before code is written, catching wrong data-model assumptions early; agent-watchdog audits another agent's work from its session or transcript; and debug-feedback-loop builds a deterministic pass/fail signal for a bug BEFORE hypothesising about causes."
    },
    {
      "name": "hardening",
      "source": "./plugins/hardening",
      "description": "Five pre-launch security gates covering the unglamorous failures that reach production. rate-limit-audit inventories every endpoint calling a paid API and every auth endpoint, then checks each actually has a limit; exposure-scan checks installed packages across npm, Go, PyPI, RubyGems and MCP servers against threat-intelligence catalogs for known-compromised releases; auth-hardening is a session, cookie, CSRF and OAuth-scope audit; webhook-reliability covers signature verification, idempotency, retry and dead letters in both directions; and privacy-audit inventories exactly what user data is collected and where it lands, checked against the code rather than the policy."
    },
    {
      "name": "reporting-comms",
      "source": "./plugins/reporting-comms",
      "description": "Six skills for turning agent output into something a person actually wants to read. html renders plans, reviews, research, and comparisons as a single self-contained HTML artifact; visual-plan and visual-recap turn text plans and git diffs into interactive documents with diagrams, file maps, and annotated code; recap-table produces before/after and what-changed tables on demand; and writing-clearly-and-concisely and human-writing tighten the prose itself, stripping AI tells, corporate register, and padding."
    },
    {
      "name": "codebase-intel",
      "source": "./plugins/codebase-intel",
      "description": "Four skills for building an accurate picture of a codebase and the libraries it depends on, before committing to a change. codebase-health surfaces complexity hotspots, churn, and bus factor when onboarding or planning a refactor; codebase-architecture-scanner generates layered architecture documentation with C4 and sequence diagrams; grill-with-docs challenges a plan against the existing domain model and sharpens terminology; and read-the-damn-docs stops guesses about third-party API behavior by going to the current documentation first."
    },
    {
      "name": "ship-pipeline",
      "source": "./plugins/ship-pipeline",
      "description": "Seven repo-agnostic skills for the ship half of the development loop. start-issue (full-issue intake including comments, prior-art check, baseline capture, branch naming), db-truth (ground schema claims in the live database before designing against them; confirm migrations actually landed after applying), prove-it (end-of-work evidence protocol — discovers what CI actually gates, runs both static gates, checks threaded values at their terminus, performs one real persistence round-trip, and emits a claim→command→result table where anything unprovable is labeled UNVERIFIED rather than assumed), review-merge-pipeline (verify → review → fix → commit → push → PR → merge in one shot, detecting the repo's integration branch instead of assuming one), deploy (production promotion with merge strategy inferred from repository history), db-migration-safety (expand-contract sequencing, idempotent SQL, batched backfills), and backup-verify (confirms backups exist AND actually restore, via a scratch branch with smoke queries and timestamped evidence). Every skill defers to a repo-local version of itself when the project defines one."
    },
    {
      "name": "work-plan",
      "source": {
        "source": "github",
        "repo": "stylusnexus/work-plan-toolkit",
        "ref": "v2026.07.23-e8b226f"
      },
      "description": "Track-aware daily planning over GitHub issues. Shared tracks (git-synced .work-plan/) optionally pinned to a canonical plan branch (plan-branch; push-track promotes a private track to it), AI clustering (group/auto-triage), coverage, plan-status doc liveness with drift detection, batched GraphQL fetches, and dependency-aware next-up with per-track ordering presets. Includes a theme-aware, accessible VS Code viewer — sidebar tree with a visibility×tier exposure badge, a repo-qualified Mermaid dependency graph, per-issue in-progress badge/toggle and dependency chips, next-up controls, proactive auto-slot suggestions with a compare-and-swap collision guard, and a Plans view with confirm-gated frontmatter writes and repository-contained plan links. Installer ownership is content-verified so unmanaged or modified launchers are preserved."
    },
    {
      "name": "defect-scan",
      "source": {
        "source": "github",
        "repo": "stylusnexus/defect-scan",
        "ref": "v1.13.0"
      },
      "description": "Language-aware defect hunter for Claude Code AND Codex. Detect stack -> triage by risk -> run real analyzers (ruff/mypy, tsc/eslint, rubocop/brakeman, +optional semgrep/gitleaks/bandit) -> reason with battle-tested patterns + 15 language profiles (python, react-typescript, ruby, go, csharp, java, kotlin, swift, objc, php, rust, yaml, shell, dart) -> report (confidence-tiered, severity/priority, gh-issue-correlated) -> optionally file deduped/labeled issues (--file-issues), apply safe fixes (--fix), or second-opinion via Codex (--cross-model). Runs on macOS/Linux/Windows (WSL/Git-Bash or PowerShell shim); model-free eval harness; extensible drop-in profiles/patterns."
    }
  ]
}

